 HOW TO MAKE A GOOD SOUP WITH WHAT REMAINS FROM BREAKFAST 
Take the remnants of a beefsteak, cut away all fat, cut the meat in small pieces, put them in a saucepan, cover your meat with cold water, put the lid half way on, let it simmer and draw half an hour, add to it two or three spoonfuls of cooked tomatoes; cut a cooked potato, a carrot sliced in two, half an onion, a small piece of cabbage,  parsley,  salt and pepper. Let it simmer two hours. If you find it short add a little cold water with your vegetables and you will have a delicious soup. --&#34;MON REPOS.&#34;  
